# GitHub-source installations

- When a GitHub source directory does not yet exist, shallow-clone only the latest commit into `~/.local/share/<application>` and retain the checkout there.
- Exceptions:
  - GitHub-sourced MCP servers: `~/.local/mcp/<server>`
  - Neovim plugins: `~/.local/share/nvim/plugins/<plugin>`
- On later runs, fetch and compare the checkout with its configured upstream before updating.
- When the upstream revision has changed, reset the checkout to that revision. Do not fast-forward pull; shallow clones break when upstream history is rewritten.
- Build and install after the initial clone, and rebuild and reinstall only when the source revision changes.
- Neovim plugins are installed by replacing `~/.config/nvim/pack/external/start/<plugin>` from the checkout when the revision changes or the live plugin directory is missing.
